Xriscos
=======

An X Window System server for the RISC OS desktop: X programs running on
other computers (Linux, the BSDs, ...) show their windows on RISC OS, and
take its keyboard and mouse. Built from xorg-server 1.19.7 (a kdrive server).

Needs RISC OS 3.5 or later and an Internet stack; developed and tested on
RISC OS 3.70 on a StrongARM Risc PC.


Starting it
-----------

Double-click !Xriscos. The X logo appears on the icon bar and the X screen
(640x480 to start with) in a window. It is display :0, listening on TCP port
6000, so from another computer:

    DISPLAY=riscpc:0 xterm &

(riscpc being this machine's name or address). Access control is off: any
computer that can reach port 6000 can use the display, so use it on a
network you trust.


The icon bar icon
-----------------

  Select       brings the X window to the front (or reopens it)
  Menu         Fullscreen   X takes over the whole screen (or Alt+Return)
               Rootless     see below; takes effect at the next start
               Quit         ends the server and its clients

Closing the X window leaves the server running.


The X window
------------

Select, Menu and Adjust are X buttons 1, 2 and 3. Clicking in the window
gives it the caret; X gets the keyboard while it has the caret. The keyboard
layout follows the RISC OS keyboard setting (UK or USA).

Resizing the window resizes the X screen. Alt+Return switches between the
window and full screen; full screen needs the desktop at X's depth (32K
colours by default, 16M with -screen WxHx24).


Rootless
--------

With Rootless ticked, there is no X screen window: each X window is a
RISC OS window of its own, moved, resized, stacked and closed by the Wimp,
which is the window manager (don't run an X one). Drag a window's bottom
right corner to resize it. The setting is kept in Choices:Xriscos.Options.


Options
-------

!Run passes its arguments on to the server, as in

    *Run <Xriscos$Dir>.!Run -rootless -screen 800x600x24

  -screen WxH[x24]   X screen size (and 24-bit depth instead of 15)
  -rootless          rootless for this run, whatever the choices say
  -norootless        the X screen in one window, likewise
  -xkb-layout L      keyboard layout (us or gb)
  -novcache          full screen: leave screen memory uncached
  -keylog            log each key and its mapping

and the usual X server options. The server writes its messages to xlog in
this directory. *Set Xriscos$NoBlockCopy 1, before starting, stops rootless
windows from scrolling with Wimp_BlockCopy.


Memory
------

!Run sets an 8000K slot. A rootless window's pixels take 2 bytes a pixel
(4 at depth 24) of it, so many large windows may need more: edit WimpSlot
in !Run.


Contents
--------

  !RunImage    the server
  SharedULib   SharedUnixLibrary, loaded if no newer one is
  xkb          precompiled keymaps
